The librarian claims that a reading program launched at the start of 2023 reversed a decline in borrowing.', 'Which choice best describes data from the table that support the librarian''s claim?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Borrowing fell from 2021 to 2022, then rose sharply in 2023 and continued to rise in 2024."},{"key":"B","text":"Borrowing was higher in 2021 than in any later year."},{"key":"C","text":"Borrowing rose steadily every year from 2021 to 2024."},{"key":"D","text":"Borrowing in 2024 was lower than borrowing in 2023."}]'::jsonb, 'A', null, 'The claim has two parts, a decline and a reversal, and choice A shows both: 6.1 to 5.4, then 7.9 and 8.3 after the program began. Choice C is the trap: it describes growth but erases the decline, and the 2022 figure contradicts it.') on conflict (id) do nothing;
• Teff is a grain that was domesticated in the Ethiopian highlands thousands of years ago.
• Its seeds are tiny: about 150 teff grains weigh as much as a single grain of wheat.
• Teff is naturally gluten-free.
• It is the main ingredient of injera, a fermented flatbread eaten daily in Ethiopia and Eritrea.
• Since the 2010s, teff flour has been sold in health-food stores in Europe and North America.', 'The student wants to emphasize the contrast between teff''s long history in one region and its recent spread elsewhere. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Teff is naturally gluten-free and is the main ingredient of injera, a fermented flatbread."},{"key":"B","text":"About 150 teff grains weigh as much as a single grain of wheat."},{"key":"C","text":"Injera, a fermented flatbread made from teff, is eaten daily in Ethiopia and Eritrea."},{"key":"D","text":"Domesticated in the Ethiopian highlands thousands of years ago, teff reached health-food stores in Europe and North America only in the 2010s."}]'::jsonb, 'D', null, 'The goal names two things, a long history in one place and a recent spread elsewhere, and only choice D puts both in one sentence with ''thousands of years ago'' against ''only in the 2010s.'' The others are true notes but address a single idea each.') on conflict (id) do nothing;
• Hedy Lamarr was a Hollywood film star in the 1930s and 1940s.
• In 1942 she and the composer George Antheil patented a ''frequency-hopping'' system to keep radio-guided torpedoes from being jammed.
• The US Navy did not adopt the system during World War II.
• Decades later, frequency-hopping principles underpinned technologies such as Bluetooth and Wi-Fi.
• Lamarr received an award from the Electronic Frontier Foundation in 1997.', 'The student wants to explain why the invention''s importance was not recognized at the time. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Hedy Lamarr, a Hollywood film star of the 1930s and 1940s, received an award from the Electronic Frontier Foundation in 1997."},{"key":"B","text":"Although Lamarr and Antheil patented frequency hopping in 1942, the Navy did not adopt it during the war, and its value became clear only decades later, when the same principles underpinned Bluetooth and Wi-Fi."},{"key":"C","text":"Frequency hopping, which Lamarr and Antheil patented in 1942, underpins Bluetooth and Wi-Fi."},{"key":"D","text":"Lamarr and Antheil designed their system to keep radio-guided torpedoes from being jammed."}]'::jsonb, 'B', null, 'Explaining why importance went unrecognized requires both the rejection at the time (the Navy did not adopt it) and the late vindication (decades later). Choice C is the trap: it links the patent to Wi-Fi but says nothing about the delay or why it happened.') on conflict (id) do nothing;

