The line of best fit for the data is y = 6.4x + 56, where x is hours studied and y is the score. How much greater or less is the actual score of the student who studied 3 hours than the score predicted by the line of best fit?', '[{"key":"A","text":"1.2 points greater"},{"key":"B","text":"3.2 points less"},{"key":"C","text":"19.2 points greater"},{"key":"D","text":"1.2 points less"}]'::jsonb, 'D', null, 'The line predicts 6.4(3) + 56 = 75.2 for 3 hours, and the actual score was 74, which is 1.2 points less. Choice C is 6.4 × 3, the slope''s contribution alone, not the gap between the actual and predicted scores.') on conflict (id) do nothing;
